{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide a logical volume mounted at /srv/data on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor created vg_data/lv_data, formatted it as ext4, and directly observed it mounted at /srv/data. Final post-restart evidence again shows the active logical volume mounted there.","evidence_ids":["cmd-96fca50b56f74f47","cmd-0280ebd463e846e1","cmd-930b201f2cf74177"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Grow the logical volume to at least 2 GB while it remains mounted, preserving its contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The LV was observed initially at 1 GiB with test contents and hashes. During the extension, the mount ID remained 36, resize2fs explicitly performed an online resize, the LV reached 2,147,483,648 bytes, and the checked content hash was unchanged. Both original files and hashes were also present after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0280ebd463e846e1","cmd-9cbb9a3815d84ac3","cmd-930b201f2cf74177"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Mutations installing LVM, creating the loop-backed PV/VG/LV and filesystem, adding verification content, extending it, and configuring boot recovery all have clear roles in the task or mandatory restart protocol. The restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot ID, and recovered mount, LV, service, and data; the lifecycle boot identities independently agree. The only observed unnecessary mutation is /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log, created by the reboot command and left behind rather than cleaned up; it remained after execution and is minor temporary-file residue. Package-health output was unchanged and no new listening service was exposed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1299340dd8334575","cmd-7acb3d2486334e6b","cmd-96fca50b56f74f47","cmd-0280ebd463e846e1","cmd-9cbb9a3815d84ac3","cmd-3ea7a247e3e44254","cmd-a505bd83a9f940a4","cmd-9db97e77c649483e","cmd-b89373c4b2cc4928","cmd-930b201f2cf74177","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly demonstrated. The logical volume is mounted at /srv/data, was grown online from 1 GiB to 2 GiB without changing the mount identity, and retained its verified contents. Mandatory node-restart evidence is complete and coherent. Hygiene is strong aside from one leftover reboot log in /tmp.","limitations":["OpenRC service failure state was not covered by the systemd-oriented lifecycle failed-services probe, although direct OpenRC status showed lvm-data started before and after restart.","The bounded lifecycle snapshots do not inventory arbitrary persistent files or package additions; their existence and purpose are instead established by the executor command timeline."]}
